---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BuildStatus from '../components/BuildStatus.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Robertas Rudys - Senior .NET Software Engineer"
  description="Resume and profile of Robertas Rudys."
>
  <h1>Robertas Rudys</h1>

  <section class="profile-sketch" aria-label="Profile summary">
    <div class="profile-sketch__row">
      <p class="profile-sketch__label">Role</p>
      <p class="profile-sketch__value">Senior .NET Software Engineer</p>
    </div>
    <div class="profile-sketch__row">
      <p class="profile-sketch__label">Email</p>
      <p class="profile-sketch__value">
        <a href="mailto:robertas.rudys+www@gmail.com"
          >robertas.rudys+www@gmail.com</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="profile-sketch__row">
      <p class="profile-sketch__label">Location</p>
      <p class="profile-sketch__value">Lithuania / EU</p>
    </div>
    <div class="profile-sketch__row">
      <p class="profile-sketch__label">Remote</p>
      <p class="profile-sketch__value">Open to Remote (EU time zones)</p>
    </div>
    <div class="profile-sketch__row">
      <p class="profile-sketch__label">Stack</p>
      <p class="profile-sketch__value">Backend (.NET, SQL, Web)</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>Profile</h2>

  <p>
    Senior .NET Software Engineer with ~7 years of professional experience
    working on data-driven and product-focused systems. Strong background in
    backend development with .NET, C#, MS SQL Server, and web development
    experience with modern frameworks.
  </p>

  <p>
    I've worked across stable product teams and fast-changing environments,
    which helped me become adaptable and pragmatic. I'm now intentionally
    focused on a long-term role in a stable product company, where I can take
    ownership, grow steadily, and deliver consistent value.
  </p>

  <h2>Core Skills</h2>

  <ul class="skills-list">
    <li>
      <strong>Backend:</strong> C#, .NET (Framework / Core / modern .NET), REST APIs
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Databases:</strong> MS SQL Server, T-SQL, data modeling, performance
      tuning
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Frontend:</strong> Angular (working knowledge), HTML/CSS, JavaScript/TypeScript
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Architecture:</strong> Monoliths, modular systems, integrations
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Practices:</strong> Code reviews, debugging legacy systems, collaboration
      in cross-functional teams
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Other:</strong> Git, CI/CD basics, cloud fundamentals (Azure - working
      knowledge)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Experience</h2>

  <h3>Senior .NET Software Engineer</h3>
  <p>Product Company (EU, Remote)<br />2026 - Present</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Building and maintaining backend services for a stable product platform
    </li>
    <li>Improving performance and reliability of core .NET services</li>
    <li>
      Partnering with product and data teams to deliver long-term roadmap work
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Senior .NET Software Engineer</h3>
  <p>Adform Lithuania<br />2025</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Engineered scalable AdTech backend services in a high-concurrency
      environment
    </li>
    <li>
      Developed and optimized mission-critical features in existing production
      codebases
    </li>
    <li>
      Collaborated within a mature engineering organization to uphold strict
      technical standards
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Senior / Software Engineer (.NET)</h3>
  <p>Ignitis Group Services Center<br />2023</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Refactored and maintained enterprise-grade .NET internal systems</li>
    <li>Extended complex codebases while ensuring stability and performance</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Software Engineer (.NET / Blockchain)</h3>
  <p>Super How<br />2021 - 2022</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Developed and deployed decentralized applications (dApps) and smart
      contract integrations
    </li>
    <li>
      Delivered end-to-end features in a fast-paced, early-stage product
      environment
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Software Engineer (.NET / SQL)</h3>
  <p>Euromonitor International<br />2018 - 2020</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Engineered data-heavy MS SQL Server solutions for international market
      research
    </li>
    <li>
      Led full-stack development initiatives using .NET and Angular for key
      product modules
    </li>
    <li>
      Maintained long-term stability of core business systems used globally
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Software Engineer (C# / Unity)</h3>
  <p>Invenis<br />2015</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Developed interactive 3D applications using C# and Unity3D</li>
    <li>Implemented core game logic and UI systems for client projects</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Independent Projects</h2>

  <h3>Founder / Product &amp; Engineering</h3>
  <p>Early-Stage Startup (Self-Initiated)<br />2024</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Initiated a startup project based on accumulated product, marketing, and
      technical knowledge
    </li>
    <li>
      Worked on early product definition, validation ideas, and technical
      direction
    </li>
    <li>Explored go-to-market strategy and team formation</li>
    <li>
      Closed the legal entity after the team did not fully materialize,
      retaining lessons learned around product scope, execution, and risk
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What I'm Looking For Next</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Stable product company</li>
    <li>Backend or .NET role</li>
    <li>Long-term collaboration and clear expectations</li>
    <li>English-first engineering environment</li>
    <li>Sustainable pace and ownership over time</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Writing</h2>

  <ul class="writing-list">
    <li><a class="touch-link" href="/blog">Blog index</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Build Status</h2>

  <BuildStatus />
</BaseLayout>
